course: dictionary
lesson: 6671
title: Obedience: doing what you are asked
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Obedience is a noun. It means doing what you are told by someone in charge, or following rules and laws. Its clues are in the sentence: «Sparta loved discipline, obedience and its army.» The Spartans valued obedience, which means following their leaders without arguing.
explain: Look at the words around a hard word. «Monks and nuns... obedience (doing as their leaders say).» The brackets explain the word straight away. Brackets, dashes and commas often give you a meaning, so check them first.
explain: One word can mean different things in different places. In church, obedience can mean following God's commands. For dogs, it means training them to follow commands, as in «obedience classes». The rest of the sentence tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Some sentences show that obedience is not always simple. «People argue how much obedience Confucius meant.» This tells you that thinkers disagree about it. When you read a sentence like this, ask yourself: what is the author really saying?
fact: Obedience is a noun, so you can show obedience or have obedience.
fact: «Obedience» means doing what you are told by someone in charge, or following rules and laws.
fact: In church, «obedience» can mean following God's commands, as Abraham and Mary did.
fact: For dogs, «obedience» means training them to follow commands: «obedience classes».
fact: A «vow of obedience» is a promise, made by monks and nuns, to do as their leaders say.
exercise: In «Monks and nuns... obedience (doing as their leaders say)», what does obedience mean? | Owning nothing of their own | Not marrying | Living by the sea | *Doing as their leaders say
exercise: Dog obedience classes teach dogs to do what? | *Follow commands | Eat only meat | Swim fast | Run in races for prizes
exercise: Which is a good example of obedience at school? | Making up your own rules | Ignoring the teacher's instructions | *Following the class rules when the teacher asks | Hiding the register
test: The vicar says our first obedience is to God. In this sentence, what does obedience mean? | Forgetting about God | Doing whatever anyone at all says | Going to the shops | Quoting, on purpose, the Bible | *Following what God asks of us
test: Which word means doing what someone in charge asks? | Curiosity | Wandering | Confusion | *Obedience
exam: Why do people argue about Confucius and obedience? | Because obedience is a colour | *Because it is not clear how much obedience he meant | Because he never spoke about rulers | Because he was a monk
